## Web Real-Time Communication Techniques

## Comparison Table

| Technique | Direction | Protocol | Latency | Complexity | Use Case |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| Short Polling | Client→Server | HTTP | High (interval-bound) | Low | Simple dashboards |
| Long Polling | Client→Server (held) | HTTP | Medium | Medium | Notifications |
| SSE / EventSource | Server→Client only | HTTP | Low | Low | Live feeds, AI streaming |
| WebSocket | Full-duplex | WS | Very low | Medium | Chat, gaming, collab |
| WebRTC | Peer-to-peer | UDP/DTLS | Ultra-low | High | Video calls, P2P |

## Decision Flow

```
Need real-time?
  Yes
    ├── Server push only (no client messages)?
    │     └── Use SSE/EventSource (simpler, HTTP-compatible)
    ├── Full bidirectional?
    │     └── Use WebSocket
    └── Audio/video or P2P?
          └── Use WebRTC
  No → Use HTTP REST
```

## Quick Reference

```javascript
// Short Polling
setInterval(() => fetch('/api/data').then(update), 3000);

// Long Polling
async function poll() {
  const r = await fetch('/api/wait');
  handle(await r.json()); poll();
}

// SSE
const es = new EventSource('/api/stream');
es.onmessage = e => handle(e.data);

// WebSocket
const ws = new WebSocket('wss://example.com');
ws.onmessage = e => handle(e.data);
ws.send(JSON.stringify({ type: 'ping' }));
```

## Server-Sent Events (SSE) / EventSource

## How SSE Works

```
Client ──→ GET /api/stream (with Accept: text/event-stream)
Server ←── 200 OK, Content-Type: text/event-stream
Server ──→ data: {"type":"update","count":42}\n\n
Server ──→ data: {"type":"update","count":43}\n\n
Server ──→ event: alert\n
           data: {"msg":"Server restarting"}\n\n
           (connection stays open)
```

## Browser API

```javascript
const eventSource = new EventSource('/api/stream');

// Default message
eventSource.onmessage = (event) => {
  const data = JSON.parse(event.data);
  updateUI(data);
};

// Named event
eventSource.addEventListener('alert', (event) => {
  showAlert(JSON.parse(event.data));
});

// Error + auto-reconnect
eventSource.onerror = () => {
  console.warn('Reconnecting...');
};

// Close
eventSource.close();
```

## SSE Wire Format

```
data: Hello world\n\n          # simple message

id: 42\n                        # last event ID (for reconnect)
data: {"count": 42}\n\n

event: notification\n           # named event
data: {"text": "Hey!"}\n\n

: this is a comment\n\n         # heartbeat (keeps connection alive)
```

## SSE Advantages

- Works through HTTP/2 multiplexing → handles 6+ SSE streams on same connection
- Automatic reconnection built into the browser
- CDN and load balancer compatible (standard HTTP)
- Much simpler server implementation than WebSocket
- Text-only (UTF-8) — good for JSON, not binary
